      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-114146 (GHSA-67wp-ghc2-fw2g) is an ASP.NET Core elevation of privilege issue: SignalR connections are not consistently bound to the identity negotiated when the connection is established, so injected messages can run Hub invocations as the victim; the fix is in Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.Connections (https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/commit/db8579880b30153dbd601fa079f49e7e3ce42e08). Microsoft lists the ASP.NET Core 9.0 runtime, including the linux-musl-x64 and linux-musl-arm64 runtime packs, as affected up to 9.0.22 and fixed in 9.0.23 (https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/security/advisories/GHSA-67wp-ghc2-fw2g, https://github.com/dotnet/announcements/issues/504, https://github.com/dotnet/core/blob/main/release-notes/9.0/9.0.23/9.0.23.md). DHI dotnet9-runtime for Alpine 3.23 builds .NET 9 for Linux from Microsoft's source release, and each build's version is the .NET runtime version it carries; 9.0.23-r0 is built from the dotnet/dotnet v9.0.124 source tag (https://github.com/dotnet/dotnet/releases/tag/v9.0.124), and its assemblies record that tag's commit, f4699d9. Scanned all 242 packages of the eleven published builds (9.0.12-r0, 9.0.13-r0, 9.0.14-r0, 9.0.15-r0, 9.0.16-r0, 9.0.17-r0, 9.0.18-r0, 9.0.20-r0, 9.0.21-r0, 9.0.22-r0 and 9.0.23-r0) for x86_64 and aarch64, including the files inside the nupkg and other zip archives they hold: every build ships ASP.NET Core 9 at its own .NET version in three places: the shared framework in aspnetcore9-runtime, the shared framework in the .NET SDK held by dotnet9-runtime-bootstrap, and the ASP.NET Core runtime pack NuGet package that dotnet9-runtime-bootstrap also holds: 9.0.12 through 9.0.22 in the earlier builds and 9.0.23 in both 9.0.23-r0 builds, and each of those copies contains Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.Connections.dll. The reference assemblies of the same name in aspnetcore9-targeting-pack, dotnet9-runtime-artifacts and the SDK's targeting pack are compile-time metadata with no implementation code. The range ends at 9.0.23-r0 because it is the first published build with the fix."
